ca-06017-bos-matter-40588.title:
Treasurer-Tax Collector's Office recommending the Board approve the following:
1) Make findings that it is appropriate to engage an independent contractor to provide Countywide banking services, as Agreement 10532 can be more economically and feasibly performed by independent contractors than County employees in accordance with County ordinance code 3.13.030(A);
2) Award Bid 2026-0100 for the purchase of banking services to the lowest responsive bidder, Bank of America;
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign, competitively procured, Agreement 10532 with Bank of America, for the provision of banking services, effective upon execution for a period of 3 years, with 2 one-year options to extend, for a total possible term of 5 years in the amount of $250,000; and
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement10532, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement. 

FUNDING: General Fund.

ca-06017-bos-matter-41365.title:
Probation Department recommending the Board:
1) Make findings in accordance with El Dorado County Ordinance Code Section 3.13.030(B) that adult and juvenile sex offender counseling services requires specialty skills and qualifications not expressly identified in County classifications; 
2) Make findings in accordance with Procurement Policy C-17 Section 3.6.G.6 that Agreement 10412 is exempt from competitive bidding because the continuity of providers will provide efficiency or critical knowledge, and other providers cannot provide;
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign Agreement 10412 with Fostering Connections, in the amount of $175,000, to commence upon execution, and end three years thereafter; and
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement 10412, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement.
 
FUNDING:  AB109 (Public Safety Realignment) (85%), Juvenile Justice Realignment Block Grant (SB 823) (15%).

ca-06017-bos-matter-41377.title:
Department of Transportation recommending the Board adopt and authorize the Chair to sign Resolution 178-2026, rescinding prior Resolution 164-2018 which established imprest accounts for the Department of Transportation in the total amount of $11,400, and reestablishing imprest cash funds in the cumulative amount of $21,400, consisting of: 
1) $21,000 for Emergency Road/Snow Operations; 
2) $200 for Department of Transportation's Development, Right-of-Way, and Environmental Unit; 
3) $100 for the Placerville Department of Transportation's Office; and 
4) $100 for the South Lake Tahoe Department of Transportation's Office.
 
FUNDING:  Road Fund.  (100% - Local)
